WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.660
Same deadline, two screens: Jan 15 and Jan 14.

2
00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:07.340
Nobody edited it.

3
00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:10.510
Stored value: "2026-01-15".

4
00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:17.910
A calendar date: no time, no zone.

5
00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:21.220
new Date("2026-01-15") → 2026-01-15T00:00:00.000Z

6
00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:27.840
Date-only form = UTC midnight. Other formats differ.

7
00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:35.280
New York shows 2026-01-14. Tokyo shows 2026-01-15.

8
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:41.660
Computed by Intl.DateTimeFormat in this fixture.

9
00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:46.990
Deadline: a calendar date. Meeting: an instant.

10
00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:51.550
Convert instants. Do not convert dates.

11
00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:59.800
Validate the date, then render it. No Date object.

12
00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:03.460
Every zone shows 2026-01-15.

13
00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:08.080
Meeting: 2026-01-15T15:00:00Z, shown per zone.

14
00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:15.480
New York 10:00. Tokyo 00:00 on the 16th.

15
00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:22.160
Named zones, not fixed offsets. DST not covered here.

16
00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:27.350
A date is not always a moment.
